  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Florida's 6th Congressional District will hold its regular election on November 3, 2026, following a special election in April 2025 that brought Republican Randy Fine to the seat. The district covers a six-county area in east-central Florida including Daytona Beach, St. Johns County, and parts of Volusia, Flagler, Putnam, and Lake counties. A new congressional map signed by Governor Ron DeSantis in May 2026 takes effect for this cycle and is being challenged in court over alleged partisan gerrymandering. The Republican primary on August 18, 2026 features incumbent Fine facing three challengers: social media personality Dan Bilzerian, retired Brigadier General Charles Gambaro, and activist Aaron Baker. On the Democratic side, Marine veteran Robert Cooper II and business owner Eric Yonce are competing for the nomination. The race has drawn national attention due to Fine's controversial rhetoric and Bilzerian's antisemitic statements.",
