      "name": "Randy Fine",
      "party": "Republican",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Randy Fine is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Florida's 6th Congressional District, having won a special election in April 2025 after Mike Waltz resigned to become National Security Advisor. A former gambling industry executive, Fine served in the Florida House of Representatives (2016-2024) and Florida Senate (2024-2025) before moving to Congress. He holds degrees from Harvard University (BA in Government, magna cum laude) and Harvard Business School (MBA, Baker Scholar). Fine has been endorsed by President Donald Trump and serves on the House Foreign Affairs and Education and Workforce Committees.",
